;; repr/cpp's native-check's negative controls (doc/GATE-SURVEY.md, GTS81 (a), "As built: GT9's controls"; bin/repr-cpp native-check,
;; arbace.repr.cpp.ncheck's judge-controls): each is a crossed pair of two files of a run's list (names as the list gives them), both
;; :same in the check. The :subject is read by the native parser and judged by the check's own comparison (`differing-items`, item by item)
;; against the clang read of the :reference (its dump), and must differ. A control with no item that differs (the comparison passes what
;; differs), or whose read is refused, fails the check; one whose files the run's list lacks (another list) is left. No control is a row of
;; results.tsv, the known file or the counts. Read with the Clojure reader.
[{:id "_control/bitfields-vs-io" :subject "bitfields.cpp" :reference "io.cpp"
  :why "the samples list (test/cpp/samples): two samples both :same in the check, other declarations"}
 {:id "_control/native-sample-pair" :subject "decls.cpp" :reference "auto.cpp"
  :why "the samples list again, a second pair, in case bitfields.cpp or io.cpp is excluded by a later known entry"}]
